# Backend Rules (server/)

Stack: Express + TypeScript + Prisma + zod + JWT. Layer rule is absolute:

```text
routes/ → controllers/ → services/ → Prisma
```

## Layers

- `routes/` — URL + middleware wiring only. No logic.
- `controllers/` — parse request, call one service, send response. Never import Prisma.
- `services/` — business logic + ALL Prisma access. Ownership checks live here.
- `middleware/` — `auth`, `requireRole`, `validate(schema)`, central error handler.
- `lib/` — prisma client singleton, jwt helpers, cloudinary, `matcher.ts`, `skills.ts` (pure).

## API contract

- Validate every mutating request with zod middleware before the controller.
- Responses: `{ data: ... }` or `{ error: { message, details? } }`; correct HTTP codes (401 unauthenticated, 403 forbidden, 404 not-found, 409 conflict).
- Never return `passwordHash` or internal errors. Production errors never include stack traces.
- Endpoint list is fixed in `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` §6 — extend the doc first if a new endpoint is needed.

## Security

- Re-check auth AND ownership server-side on every protected handler (see `docs/SECURITY.md` §2 matrix).
- Uploads: PDF only, ≤ 5 MB, memory storage, server-generated Cloudinary public IDs.
- No raw SQL (`$queryRaw`) without an ADR.

## Quality

- Pure functions (matcher, keyword extraction, CSV escaping) in `lib/` with unit tests.
- Every new endpoint gets an integration test: happy path + 401 + 403 + validation failure.
